    "attribution": "Locally generated with authorized ROMs. English T.1 DMD captions visually checked against native snapshots; cp_15 sensor snapshots 7 through 24 have identical pixel SHA-256 to the independently inspected cp_16 snapshots. Public writes/readback are host stimuli, never ROM evidence. 32 (normalized opto) and 52 (ordinary switch) are active-high controls; right jab38 is active-low; rope64 and scoop61/62 active-high. Synthetic motor model only establishes boot; feedback was suspended before step7 and no host feedback events follow. Model script SHA-256 b8e2be1ddfb7151bb6da33ea34caf5e524fc006b3585e3abc7db331d9e630701; VPX embedded script SHA-256 0060c3892e5b35d154d2fb5325284658787121b81111e6ba3d267d6d8bc66a6c. No physical cam sizes/speeds, hardware quantities, GI assignment or other variants are proved. Upper button steps25-30 can cause automatic lower-flipper EOS captions and are excluded from these polarity observations. Exact external directory manifest checkpoint-polarity/manifest.json SHA-256 6b7a19dd5d637b276e1731fa167bcb7e7d1d916cf4fc6dd333697bb453233bac, files-array digest fd63e0687d1cc54ec4594d69e47f3087d1711eb4ccd6a9854e69de2154ace5d5; contains raw trace, copied scenario, DMD images and isolated mutable state, with no ROM bytes.",
